# The programs of the relay

Stage `i` is a real program in a real language.  Each program is

```
pre  @ <the payload, in this stage's own notation> @  post
```

and the payload encodes the five blocks (`pre`, `post`, and the three pieces of
the shape) of *every* stage, so any program can print any program — the next one
in the cycle, itself, or any other.  Running the stages in turn takes the text
all the way around and back to where it started (`relay_cycle`).

